Z||000002||dlancer407||07-09-2001||04:39 PM||||I think that would be a great idea. I live in Colerain Twp. and I would be very interested.||||reg||14
Z||000003||FieroPerformance||07-10-2001||12:57 AM||||*BUMP*<P>C'Mon you guys. There has to be more interest than this. I see Fieros all the time around here. This is a great place for a club. I guess we could start one with 3 members but that might not be as fun.<P>-Charlie<BR>jackalrr@hotmail.com<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||fieroburton||07-10-2001||01:09 AM||||we could start a 3 member club . make some club jackets and hats and a bimonthly cruse in. then when they put out the new fiero parts book we would be in it then more would join and word would get out! I still say go with it ! <P>and yes,your right there is a lot of fieros in Cincinnati ,that's why we need a good club.||||reg||14
Z||000005||blkcofy||07-10-2001||01:56 AM||||I'd be interested.  I just found out about this forum.  I've been participating in a forum regarding my other car (Contour SVT) and have recently started to rebuild my Fiero.  I've got a 1987 GT.  I've had it since 1990; bought it from my Dad (original owner) after graduating from college.  I just couldn't seem to part with it.  It's got about 73M miles and has been garaged for the last 5 years.  I started it up last week and after replacing the battery it started right up.  It's been driven about 1500 miles the last 5 years.  I'd like to get it back to good running order and use it on a regular basis for the summer.  My dream is to find a place to make it a convertible.  I'm just excited that there's an active forum for the car.  I'm glad I kept it!||||reg||1
Z||000006||tgowens||07-10-2001||02:18 AM||||I was going to start a club when I was back there but didn't have much local interest. It seems there a lot more Fiero owners finding their way to the forum now that there was a years ago. I did start the club though but I brought it to CA with me when I came out here -- I designed the web site for it with a "generic" name so it was easy to move it......you can see it at  <A HREF="http://www.cfog.org" TARGET=_blank>www.cfog.org</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||dlancer407||07-10-2001||10:38 AM||||I know I have seen Three or Four Fiero's at local shows and cruisein's here in town this year. I also own a Javelin AMX and when I take it to shows, most of the time I am the only AMC car there. Till the last couple of years you did not see any Fiero's at shows. I think that if you start a club and our cars start to go to more shows and cruises the number of members will increase.||||reg||1
Z||000008||blkcofy||07-10-2001||09:03 PM||||Questions from the new guy.  My fiero has sat undisturbed and garaged for the last 24 months.  I've gotten it started, and have driven it around a bit.  It idles very rough, so I assume I need to get a serious tune up since it's sat for so long.  I'm in need of a good exhaust system, and was looking at The Fiero Store at the Ocelot system.  Any advice on exhaust systems?  The big question is what are the main things (a checklist if you will) that I should be checking, to make sure everything is working properly.  Should I have all the liquids drained and replaced?  Is there a GOOD performance shop or garage in the Cinci area that anyone would recommend to give it a looksy?  I've got a wish list a arm long of how I want to upgrade my fiero, but I think the first thing is to get it running smoothly, before I start adding stuff.  What do you guys/gals think?  My other car is a Contour SVT (which I love) but I can see one day selling that car and it makes little sense to put alot more money into it in aftermarket stuff.  I've already spent a good $6,000 in tires, audio, aesthetics, exhaust, ect.  BUT the fiero, which I don't think I'd EVER part with, is another story.  Since finding this forum, I now have a sense of all the possibilities for this car.  Any advice you folks can give me would be appreciated.||||reg||10
Z||000009||dlancer407||07-10-2001||09:25 PM||||Hi blkcofy; Welcome to the forum and welcome to Fiero ownership. I am a new member myself as I joined the forum last month after I bought my 85 GT coupe. The first thing that comes to mind with your car running rought is that you might have bad gas in the tank.I just had some recall work done at Walker Pontiac in Tri County. They did a really good job on my car but I don't know about taking it there all the time. I to would be interested to know if anyone here in town can recommend a good repair place.<BR>                              Dennis||||reg||6
Z||000010||BENGAL4||07-10-2001||10:08 PM||||Well, first of all, I would be interested in a Cincy Fiero club. I think there is enough interest to get one started. Second, blkcofy, you should try to do the work your self. I had people work on mine the first year I had it. I got tired of paying $60.00 labor. Once I jumped into it, it wasn't too hard. Also when you get stuck, and you will. This forum is awesome for getting the right information and learning the shortcuts.<P>Good luck,<P>Bill<BR>86GT<BR>3800 Series II S/C ||||reg||1
Z||000011||blkcofy||07-10-2001||11:34 PM||||Thanks guys.  I just found a "long-term" maintenance schedule from another fiero website.  If anyone is interested, I'll post the link. I'm going to replace all the fluids and take it in for a complete tuneup.  Bengal4, your right about trying to do the work myself.  The fiero engine is so dang hard to manuvure around though.  I can't get to all six plugs, plus I think one is rusted in.  I'll try again before I take it in.  Did you do the engine swap (3800) yourself?||||reg||1
Z||000012||BENGAL4||07-11-2001||12:39 AM||||No, I didn't do the swap. I could have done the mechanical part, but I needed an expert for the electrical. On my 2.8, I replaced and repaired the following over the last few years.<P>ENGINE<P>brakes.<BR>water pump.<BR>timing chain and gears.<BR>Ocelot exhaust.<BR>ignition module. (carry a spare module).<BR>tune up.<BR> Remove the deck lid and you will have those plugs out in no time. Just mark where the brackets go and it lines right up.<BR>Power pulley.<BR>ADS chip. Don't waste your money if your thinking of a chip. Didn't feel any differnce.<P><BR>INTERIOR<BR>Mr Mikes leather seats. (Easy to do).<BR>new carpet.<BR>New interior paint.<P>You can do it.<P>Bill<BR>3800 Series II S/C<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000013||FieroPerformance||07-11-2001||01:24 AM||||Alright. I am in if we can get a club going. If you want to join the new Cincinnati Fiero club email me at jackalrr@hotmail.com  just include some basic contact info and something about yourself and your car. I will look into getting a web site set up. I can make it no problem but I don't have a credit card to pay for hosting. I know where we can get hosting for $12 a year and register a domain for $8 a year.<P>Anyway send me an email.<P>-Charlie<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000014||tgowens||07-11-2001||01:25 AM||||blkcofy, you can get to all of the plugs if you will remove the decklid first - it makes it a lot easier.......four 13mm bolts, a 10mm holding the ground wire on the left side and the plug on the right (deck release, trunk light, etc).<P>Use a stubby ratchet with a short extension and a swivel head spark plug socket and it makes the job so much easier.<P>you should change the plugs, wires, rotor and dist. cap. If you want to go further you can change the ignition module and pick up coil as well. The coils themselves are notorious for going out too so you might want to change that also......<P>Other than that, change the fluids and belts (since it has been sitting for two years!).....<P>Bengal4 knows quite a bit about the Fiero as well as 87ECO5, Boilermaker, ChadMan, WilliamThornIII, and quite a few others around Cincinnati.<P>If you need a web site done, let me know.....I would be glad to help.......I have a fond attachment for that area as I lived there for quite a number of years.<P>Bill, this is a note for you. I will be back there again right after the show in Williamsburg and will definitely get in touch with you and the rest of the group there! Scott is going to do some minor work on one of my '87GT's that I have there in northern KY and I will follow up on it when I get back there..........<P>Thanks to you all (most of the above mentioned people) for watching out for my car and daughter (emphasis on car.........) while she is driving it........<P><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/index.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>                   <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/3GTS_SIG.gif">                    </A>||||reg||1
Z||000015||BENGAL4||07-11-2001||11:44 PM||||Terry,<P>Look forward to seeing you then. 2m4DALES, bash is the weekend of the 11th. Had a great time last year and Mansfield isn't that far away. Charlie as for the club, let me know what I can do to help.<P>Bill<BR>86GT<BR>3800 Series II S/C||||reg||10
